~ guardian
do start_talking()
Guardian: You came the whole way.
Guardian: The barricade. The ledge. The stones in the dark wood, in the order the pages gave you.
Guardian: Step for step. He did not miss one either.
Guardian: [[He sat where you are standing.|He stayed four days. Then he stopped writing.|I have been waiting a long time to be asked.]]
do stop_talking()
=> END

~ altar
A low stone, worn round at the edges, with a spiral cut into its face. The cut is deeper than weather would make it.
Something is set into the groove that is not stone. It is cold, and it is the only thing here that is not pale.
=> END

~ camp
A groundsheet, a ring of cold stones, a lantern with no oil left in it. Everything is laid out neatly, and nothing has been packed.
=> END

~ stone
A hooded figure cut from one piece, facing in. Where the face should be there is only the hood.
=> END
